cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PLIERS: a configurable pipeline for leakage-aware protein-ligand interaction benchmarking"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ilya
    family-names: Senatorov
    email: ilya.senatorov@helmholtz-hips.de
    affiliation: Helmholtz Institute for Pharmaceutical Research Saarland
repository-code: "https://github.com/kalininalab/pliers"
url: "https://pliers-bio.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  PLIERS - Protein-Ligand Interaction Evaluation, Representation and Splitting - turns
  the preparation of protein-ligand interaction benchmarks into configuration. It
  represents proteins as residue-level contact graphs built from 3D structures - one
  node per residue, edges between residues whose C-alpha atoms fall within a distance
  cutoff - or as ESM-1b sequence embeddings, and ligands as molecular graphs, encoding
  both with graph neural networks. It ships a reproducible Snakemake pipeline that turns
  protein structures and interaction tables into ready-to-train graph datasets under
  five split protocols, and scores every run against label-only baselines so that
  performance attributable to dataset composition is separated from the rest.
keywords:
  - protein-ligand interaction
  - graph neural networks
  - protein contact graph
  - structural bioinformatics
  - data leakage
license: MIT
version: 4.0.0
